WEBVTT

1
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.108
It's hard to explain.

2
00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:05.507
It's hard to explain myself.

3
00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:07.908
But I never tell lies.

4
00:01:07.977 --> 00:01:10.568
Everything I say is true,

5
00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:13.075
even when
I don't say a thing.

6
00:01:22.477 --> 00:01:26.602
Someone always has to die first
before anything happens.

7
00:01:26.677 --> 00:01:30.166
Otherwise life just goes on
as if there's no problem.

8
00:01:30.243 --> 00:01:34.007
No. Someone always
has to die first.

9
00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.574
And then everyone
suddenly wakes up.

10
00:01:44.344 --> 00:01:46.071
But it's too late then.

11
00:01:55.511 --> 00:01:58.477
That's why
someone had to die.

12
00:03:49.778 --> 00:03:54.267
Every morning I play my game
from 5:.45 till 6:.33.

13
00:03:54.344 --> 00:03:56.333
Always.

14
00:03:57.377 --> 00:03:59.865
I've now reached level 80.

15
00:03:59.944 --> 00:04:02.001
If you don't know
what that means,

16
00:04:02.077 --> 00:04:04.668
it's just... high.

17
00:04:06.311 --> 00:04:09.005
It means you're strong,

18
00:04:09.077 --> 00:04:11.134
respected in the world.

19
00:04:12.844 --> 00:04:14.900
Hundreds of thousands
of people online.

20
00:04:16.711 --> 00:04:21.336
But for more than a year,

21
00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.876
I've only been playing
with her.

22
00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.740
REMEMBER, PRlNCESS MAY BE
A MAN lN REAL LlFE

23
00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.835
YOU ARE YOU

24
00:05:02.644 --> 00:05:05.633
GLAD YOU ARE YOU TOO

25
00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.076
In games you can be whoever
and whatever you like.

26
00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.776
Here you can only be
one person--

27
00:05:19.843 --> 00:05:24.139
the jerk you see
in the mirror.

28
00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:27.109
I have to teach him
everything.

29
00:05:27.177 --> 00:05:29.109
For example, I have to
teach him to laugh.

30
00:05:29.177 --> 00:05:31.268
People like that.

31
00:05:31.344 --> 00:05:35.106
To "give them a smile,"
as they say,

32
00:05:35.177 --> 00:05:38.939
which means smiling when really
there's nothing to smile about.

33
00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:49.169
That's how you create
your own avatar.

34
00:05:49.244 --> 00:05:51.904
20 seconds
for my hands...

35
00:05:54.611 --> 00:05:56.576
and 15 for my hair.

36
00:06:07.711 --> 00:06:11.007
You're as strong as
your weapons and tools.

37
00:06:11.078 --> 00:06:13.168
My heart rate meter,
for example,

38
00:06:13.244 --> 00:06:16.369
to keep track of my heart,
as they say,

39
00:06:16.444 --> 00:06:19.171
for when I get nervous.

40
00:06:19.244 --> 00:06:22.472
Not that it makes me
less nervous,

41
00:06:22.544 --> 00:06:26.374
but now I can see exactly
how nervous I am.

42
00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.471
My mother.
Now she's going to say,

43
00:06:36.543 --> 00:06:39.203
- "Good morning, Ben."
- Good morning, Ben.

44
00:06:39.277 --> 00:06:42.471
People say that whether
it's a good morning or not.

45
00:06:42.544 --> 00:06:44.134
"Good morning, Mom."

46
00:06:44.211 --> 00:06:46.370
People never say,
"Bad morning."

47
00:06:46.443 --> 00:06:48.932
Did you sleep well, son?

48
00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.772
"Really well, Mom.

49
00:06:51.843 --> 00:06:54.810
It's nice of you to ask.
Thank you."

50
00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.876
Have you seen
my troll, Ben?

51
00:06:58.944 --> 00:07:02.342
My brother Jonas.
He's still small.

52
00:07:02.411 --> 00:07:04.604
I have to be
his big brother and all.

53
00:07:04.678 --> 00:07:07.803
Trolls don't have horses.

54
00:07:07.878 --> 00:07:12.639
But somehow I never seem
to know how to.

55
00:07:19.044 --> 00:07:21.670
Calm down, Ben.
Calm down.

56
00:07:21.743 --> 00:07:23.334
Easy now, Ben.

57
00:07:23.411 --> 00:07:25.070
Okay?

58
00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.133
Don't take
any of it to heart.

59
00:07:31.777 --> 00:07:33.607
"l won't, Mom."

60
00:07:33.678 --> 00:07:36.838
I won't, Mom.
I won't take heart.

61
00:07:36.911 --> 00:07:38.570
Won't take it to heart.

62
00:07:39.945 --> 00:07:42.466
You are allowed
to take heart, son.

63
00:07:46.276 --> 00:07:48.674
Use your head,
don't get worked up.

64
00:07:48.743 --> 00:07:50.902
Give me a kiss.

65
00:07:50.977 --> 00:07:52.238
Go on.

66
00:07:59.443 --> 00:08:01.841
I've also got a weapon
for fighting noise--

67
00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.933
other noise, but nicer.

68
00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.408
Nicer noise.

69
00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.677
I've got to use my head.

70
00:08:30.744 --> 00:08:33.539
Think ahead
and think a-heart.

71
00:08:33.611 --> 00:08:36.907
Be prepared, be forewarned.
Forewarned is forearmed.

72
00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:45.336
It's all a matter
of planning, of strategy.

73
00:08:55.911 --> 00:09:00.605
I can't say I was taken totally
by surprise, but...

74
00:09:00.678 --> 00:09:03.905
it just proved that--

75
00:09:03.977 --> 00:09:08.466
that everything that'd happened
up till now wasn't right.

76
00:09:08.543 --> 00:09:10.975
Before you do
something like that,

77
00:09:11.044 --> 00:09:14.272
things must be--

78
00:09:14.344 --> 00:09:18.003
it simply
proved to me that

79
00:09:18.077 --> 00:09:22.010
things had just gone too far.
Way too far.

80
00:09:28.711 --> 00:09:30.676
People are strange.

81
00:09:31.878 --> 00:09:34.435
They talk
and talk and talk.

82
00:09:36.744 --> 00:09:38.801
And they drink
each other's saliva.

83
00:09:41.044 --> 00:09:42.510
All I can do is watch

84
00:09:42.578 --> 00:09:45.442
and copy them,
imitate them.

85
00:09:47.444 --> 00:09:49.909
Everything
I'll never learn.

86
00:10:00.377 --> 00:10:02.968
Because there was always
something the matter...

87
00:10:09.244 --> 00:10:11.107
with me and with my hand.

88
00:10:11.177 --> 00:10:12.404
Throw it to someone.

89
00:10:12.477 --> 00:10:14.841
This is getting
out of hand!

90
00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.299
- Wrong.
- What's wrong with you?

91
00:10:22.377 --> 00:10:24.969
I'm the man
who's always wrong,

92
00:10:25.045 --> 00:10:28.977
but no one
could tell me exactly

93
00:10:29.044 --> 00:10:31.101
how to be right.

94
00:10:38.644 --> 00:10:41.202
Hi, you faggots!

95
00:10:42.244 --> 00:10:45.404
Pat's got a new girlfriend.

96
00:10:45.477 --> 00:10:47.635
Sit down, darling.

97
00:10:47.711 --> 00:10:51.973
Not bad, eh? When an old girl's
in heat, sparks can fly.

98
00:10:52.044 --> 00:10:55.477
Do you know what your hand
in her knickers feels like?

99
00:10:55.544 --> 00:10:57.373
I don't want to know.

100
00:10:57.443 --> 00:11:00.705
Have you ever given
a horse a lump of sugar?

101
00:11:02.578 --> 00:11:04.669
Bogaert and Desmet.

102
00:11:04.744 --> 00:11:06.709
I'm their best friend.

103
00:11:08.244 --> 00:11:10.641
At least,
that's what they say.

104
00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:14.837
Oh, there's Benny,
our best friend.

105
00:11:14.911 --> 00:11:16.842
Our alien from Pluto.

106
00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:21.037
Living proof that man
descended from mussels.

107
00:11:21.111 --> 00:11:23.406
- Mussels?
- Hi, Benny-Boy.

108
00:11:23.477 --> 00:11:26.034
The man from Mars!
Hi!

109
00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:28.838
Whitney Houston
for Benny-Boy. Over.

110
00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:32.070
Come in, Benny-boy, over.
Over, Benny-Boy.

111
00:11:32.144 --> 00:11:34.134
Do you read me?
Hey, Benny-Boy.

112
00:11:34.212 --> 00:11:36.802
Masturbation
makes you deaf!

113
00:11:36.877 --> 00:11:38.900
Is anyone home?

114
00:11:38.977 --> 00:11:41.409
Deaf.

115
00:11:41.477 --> 00:11:43.102
Why did they always
come up with that?

116
00:11:43.177 --> 00:11:45.768
If I sat there
playing quietly,

117
00:11:45.843 --> 00:11:48.968
they thought my ears
weren't working.

118
00:11:52.743 --> 00:11:54.903
The doctor said
I could hear

119
00:11:54.977 --> 00:11:56.910
perfectly well
but I didn't listen.

120
00:11:56.978 --> 00:11:59.307
He doesn't listen.

121
00:11:59.377 --> 00:12:03.399
Then they thought there was something
wrong with my eyes.

122
00:12:03.476 --> 00:12:04.999
Can you see what
those letters are?

123
00:12:05.077 --> 00:12:07.475
- Yes.
- Yes.

124
00:12:07.544 --> 00:12:10.305
Can you tell me
what those are?

125
00:12:10.377 --> 00:12:12.206
Yes.

126
00:12:12.277 --> 00:12:15.243
The idea is that you tell me
what the letters are.

127
00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.474
C-O-H-z-v,
S-z-N-D-C,

128
00:12:18.544 --> 00:12:22.340
v-k-C-N-R,
k-C-R-H-N,

129
00:12:22.411 --> 00:12:27.106
v-O-R-k,
R-H-S-O-N, k-S-v-R-H.

130
00:12:28.377 --> 00:12:32.968
He always
looked away as a baby.

131
00:12:33.044 --> 00:12:34.976
He never looked at me.

132
00:12:35.044 --> 00:12:37.374
He always looked
through me.

133
00:12:37.444 --> 00:12:41.604
Think of them as a computer that is
configured differently.

134
00:12:41.678 --> 00:12:43.269
They see everything.

135
00:12:43.344 --> 00:12:46.242
They see every leaf
extremely clearly,

136
00:12:46.311 --> 00:12:47.777
but they don't see
the tree.

137
00:12:47.844 --> 00:12:50.935
They literally can't see
the wood for the trees.

138
00:12:54.211 --> 00:12:57.177
The big picture--
that's what it's all about.

139
00:12:57.244 --> 00:13:01.040
You have to try
to see the big picture

140
00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:04.565
and see that
they don't see you.

141
00:13:12.911 --> 00:13:14.967
- Look where you're walking.
- Retard.

142
00:13:18.511 --> 00:13:20.000
Look where you're walking.

143
00:13:20.078 --> 00:13:21.566
Retard.

144
00:13:23.212 --> 00:13:24.938
Whitney Houston
for Benny-Boy--

145
00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.533
we have a problem.

146
00:13:28.077 --> 00:13:31.009
For Benny-Boy,
the man from Mars.

147
00:13:50.844 --> 00:13:53.810
There are a couple every year.

148
00:13:53.878 --> 00:13:55.366
Always on their own
in the playground.

149
00:13:55.444 --> 00:13:57.841
It breaks my heart
to see them,

150
00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.570
but what can you do?
You can't nanny them.

151
00:14:00.644 --> 00:14:03.542
You can't hold their hand.

152
00:14:03.611 --> 00:14:06.077
Not now, that's for sure.

153
00:14:06.145 --> 00:14:10.372
I wanted my son to go
to an ordinary school.

154
00:14:10.444 --> 00:14:14.206
My wife-- my ex-wife--

155
00:14:14.277 --> 00:14:16.266
and I sometimes
argued about it.

156
00:14:18.044 --> 00:14:22.374
But he was much smarter than some
of the other kids there.

157
00:14:22.444 --> 00:14:24.569
10 times smarter.

158
00:14:25.378 --> 00:14:26.570
An understandable question.

159
00:14:26.644 --> 00:14:28.701
Where is God?
Where is He?

160
00:14:28.778 --> 00:14:32.142
Where is this man
with His long grey beard?

161
00:14:32.212 --> 00:14:35.006
With all the wars, the poverty
and the injustice...

162
00:14:35.077 --> 00:14:36.805
where is God?

163
00:14:36.878 --> 00:14:39.037
People asked themselves

164
00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:41.575
the same question
in Jesus's time.

165
00:14:41.643 --> 00:14:44.201
Jesus was hanging there
on the cross

166
00:14:44.277 --> 00:14:46.039
and they said, "Jesus,

167
00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.599
why don't
you do something?

168
00:14:47.677 --> 00:14:49.701
If your dad is
boss of the universe,

169
00:14:49.778 --> 00:14:51.801
if you can raise
someone from the dead,

170
00:14:51.878 --> 00:14:53.934
it's child's play for you.

171
00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.601
Click clack and you're free."

172
00:14:55.678 --> 00:14:58.508
Jesus, himself, wondered too.

173
00:14:58.578 --> 00:15:00.736
What does
the New Testament say?

174
00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:04.640
At the ninth hour,
Jesus cried with a loud voice,

175
00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:08.905
"My God, my God,
why hast Thou forsaken me?"

176
00:15:08.978 --> 00:15:12.808
At that moment Jesus
himself wonders that too.

177
00:15:12.878 --> 00:15:14.503
He is so humiliated,

178
00:15:14.577 --> 00:15:18.170
dispirited, disheartened,

179
00:15:18.245 --> 00:15:20.732
that Jesus himself
doubts God.

180
00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.402
He lets go.

181
00:15:23.477 --> 00:15:28.103
In fact,
Jesus commits suicide.

182
00:15:28.178 --> 00:15:32.200
Until he rises from the dead.
Until the resurrection.

183
00:15:32.277 --> 00:15:34.368
And so God--

184
00:15:34.444 --> 00:15:36.535
God damn it, Bogaert!

185
00:15:36.611 --> 00:15:38.577
Leave Ben alone!

186
00:15:38.644 --> 00:15:42.077
It's not the first time
I've had to tell you this!

187
00:15:42.144 --> 00:15:44.303
You're going to
be in trouble!

188
00:15:44.378 --> 00:15:46.570
Ben's just different
from you,

189
00:15:46.644 --> 00:15:50.474
from the below-average
members of the class.

190
00:15:50.544 --> 00:15:53.066
Fortunately for him,
if you ask me!

191
00:15:53.144 --> 00:15:55.838
But you obviously find it
very difficult

192
00:15:55.911 --> 00:15:57.877
to accept that someone
is different.

193
00:15:57.945 --> 00:16:00.274
Or is there something
you want to share with us?

194
00:16:00.344 --> 00:16:02.310
Maybe your thoughts
on the text

195
00:16:02.377 --> 00:16:06.332
you no doubt studied
in detail last night?

196
00:16:06.411 --> 00:16:11.037
- Yeah, okay.
- Right.

197
00:16:11.111 --> 00:16:13.008
We're dying of curiosity.

198
00:16:14.278 --> 00:16:17.175
Does anyone know
what Jesus said

199
00:16:17.244 --> 00:16:19.369
when they took him down
from the cross?

200
00:16:20.678 --> 00:16:24.474
"Hey! My feet first!"

201
00:16:24.544 --> 00:16:27.942
That joke's grown
really long whiskers.

202
00:16:28.011 --> 00:16:29.976
My God,
why hast Thou forsaken me?

203
00:16:30.044 --> 00:16:33.499
I ask myself the same question
numerous times a day.

204
00:16:36.311 --> 00:16:39.175
Whoa whoa whoa!
Hey! Calm down!

205
00:16:39.244 --> 00:16:40.801
Take it easy.

206
00:16:42.311 --> 00:16:45.505
Don't let them
push you around, Ben.

207
00:16:45.578 --> 00:16:48.067
Keep your cool.

208
00:16:49.344 --> 00:16:52.367
kids like him
don't stand a chance.

209
00:16:52.444 --> 00:16:54.433
They're easy prey.

210
00:16:54.511 --> 00:16:58.534
They once stuck
a bandage over his mouth

211
00:16:58.611 --> 00:17:01.543
and told him the headmaster
had said they had to.

212
00:17:01.611 --> 00:17:05.475
He walked round all day
with the bandage over his mouth.

213
00:17:05.544 --> 00:17:08.305
He always brought
a packed lunch with him,

214
00:17:08.377 --> 00:17:13.002
but he never managed
to eat it.

215
00:17:13.077 --> 00:17:16.043
But what are
you supposed to do?

216
00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.837
What we always do--
too little. Nothing.

217
00:17:21.344 --> 00:17:24.106
Here's our favorite boy.
Well, Benny-Boy?

218
00:17:24.178 --> 00:17:25.575
Our Boy Jesus.

219
00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:28.042
Leave him alone, guys.

220
00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.940
Fuck off,
Freddy faggot.

221
00:17:30.011 --> 00:17:33.136
It can't be easy, being different,
eh, Benny-Boy?

222
00:17:33.212 --> 00:17:36.644
Whoa!

223
00:17:36.711 --> 00:17:40.109
Better than average, eh?

224
00:17:40.178 --> 00:17:41.871
In fact, we should
look up to you.

225
00:17:41.944 --> 00:17:43.808
You're the man!

226
00:17:48.244 --> 00:17:50.177
Calm down.

227
00:17:50.245 --> 00:17:53.540
Don't get worked up.
Don't get worked up.

228
00:17:53.611 --> 00:17:55.872
Just stay calm.

229
00:17:59.377 --> 00:18:01.070
Smile.

230
00:18:01.144 --> 00:18:04.668
They said
to keep on smiling.

231
00:18:04.744 --> 00:18:09.142
Then it'll stop.
They'll stop.

232
00:18:25.544 --> 00:18:27.635
Movie time!

233
00:18:30.744 --> 00:18:32.039
Action.

234
00:19:04.611 --> 00:19:07.009
Faggot!

235
00:19:07.077 --> 00:19:09.475
Loser!

236
00:19:15.177 --> 00:19:17.143
Faggot!

237
00:19:18.811 --> 00:19:20.538
Loser!

238
00:20:26.811 --> 00:20:29.073
Look at me, son.

239
00:20:37.643 --> 00:20:39.735
If you don't tell me,

240
00:20:39.811 --> 00:20:42.709
how am I supposed
to know, vertriest?

241
00:20:50.911 --> 00:20:53.638
Well, well!
Look who's here.

242
00:20:53.711 --> 00:20:55.177
My favorite clients.

243
00:20:55.245 --> 00:20:58.699
- The 10th visit is free.
- Do you know why you're here?

244
00:20:58.778 --> 00:21:03.005
- I don't know.
- You really have no idea?

245
00:21:03.077 --> 00:21:05.339
Is it a quiz?

246
00:21:05.411 --> 00:21:07.537
Do you think
it's funny, Desmet?

247
00:21:09.244 --> 00:21:11.938
To be honest, I don't think
it's the least bit funny.

248
00:21:12.011 --> 00:21:15.306
Apparently you have been--

249
00:21:15.377 --> 00:21:18.468
how shall I put it?
--bullying vertriest.

250
00:21:18.544 --> 00:21:21.033
We teased him,
we didn't bully him.

251
00:21:21.111 --> 00:21:22.804
We do it
to each other too.

252
00:21:22.878 --> 00:21:26.002
But a normal person realizes
it's only in fun, sir.

253
00:21:28.145 --> 00:21:33.236
We try to treat him
normally,

254
00:21:33.311 --> 00:21:36.402
but normality doesn't come
easy for him.

255
00:21:36.477 --> 00:21:40.933
We're not the ones throwing chairs
through windows, sir.

256
00:21:41.011 --> 00:21:43.637
It's not easy
for us either.

257
00:21:43.711 --> 00:21:47.507
That'll do. Save the act
for the playground!

