Hello, Mommy.

520
00:43:59.512 --> 00:44:01.841
I'm in the park
with my friends.

521
00:44:01.912 --> 00:44:04.604
Leave a message
after the beep. Bye.

522
00:44:04.678 --> 00:44:07.304
Bye, Mommy.
Oops, mailbox.

523
00:44:07.378 --> 00:44:09.640
Let me know
where you are, okay?

524
00:44:09.712 --> 00:44:13.803
Don't you mind being
stalked, Benny-boy?

525
00:44:13.878 --> 00:44:16.810
Always having to listen
to bullshit from your mother?

526
00:44:16.878 --> 00:44:19.572
I'll keep your phone,
eh, Benny-Boy?

527
00:44:19.645 --> 00:44:21.507
What do you think?

528
00:44:38.279 --> 00:44:42.370
- Easy! Easy with the crucifix!
- You are mad after all!

529
00:44:44.178 --> 00:44:46.610
Hey, Benny, telephone.

530
00:44:46.679 --> 00:44:48.645
It's Mommy.
Aren't you going to answer it?

531
00:44:48.712 --> 00:44:51.507
It's Mommy.
She'll come and get you.

532
00:44:51.579 --> 00:44:53.408
Come on, Ben.
Answer your phone.

533
00:45:02.512 --> 00:45:04.000
My buddy Benny-Boy.

534
00:45:04.078 --> 00:45:07.669
You crazy Martian!
We're not taking you with us again!

535
00:45:07.744 --> 00:45:11.040
And to think we had
a present for you as well.

536
00:45:11.112 --> 00:45:14.168
Look, this is only
for our best friends.

537
00:45:14.245 --> 00:45:16.870
It's a little pill
that has a big effect.

538
00:45:16.945 --> 00:45:19.809
It's called a Superman.
Superman.

539
00:45:19.878 --> 00:45:21.401
Open your mouth.

540
00:45:26.378 --> 00:45:28.344
There's a smiley on it,
for people like you

541
00:45:28.412 --> 00:45:30.775
who never laugh.
Want it?

542
00:45:33.811 --> 00:45:36.334
Some water to
wash it down.

543
00:45:36.412 --> 00:45:37.935
You'll feel just
like Superman!

544
00:45:38.012 --> 00:45:41.944
There! Now swallow.

545
00:45:44.378 --> 00:45:47.538
The first one's free
because you're our friend.

546
00:45:47.612 --> 00:45:50.373
It'll do you good.
You won't be so aggressive any more.

547
00:45:50.444 --> 00:45:52.035
Here.

548
00:45:52.111 --> 00:45:55.544
So you know what time it is when you go
whining to the fatmaster.

549
00:46:05.111 --> 00:46:07.135
I don't believe this!

550
00:46:07.213 --> 00:46:09.337
Jesus Christ!

551
00:46:11.079 --> 00:46:12.374
I don't believe it!

552
00:46:12.445 --> 00:46:14.343
Phone me, please.

553
00:46:15.945 --> 00:46:17.673
What's that, Mom?

554
00:46:17.745 --> 00:46:21.438
Nothing, son.
It's nothing.

555
00:46:21.512 --> 00:46:23.000
Let's go and look
for Ben.

556
00:46:38.245 --> 00:46:39.938
Damn it.

557
00:46:40.011 --> 00:46:42.500
God damn it!

558
00:46:44.745 --> 00:46:46.642
Damn!

559
00:46:46.712 --> 00:46:48.507
Damn me!

560
00:47:07.278 --> 00:47:09.744
Where are you?
Where are you?

561
00:48:33.945 --> 00:48:37.002
Feel.

562
00:48:37.078 --> 00:48:39.544
Feel me, Ben.

563
00:48:50.345 --> 00:48:52.811
Ben.

564
00:48:57.978 --> 00:49:00.808
You have to learn
to feel

565
00:49:00.878 --> 00:49:03.344
if you want
to learn to feel good.

566
00:49:27.711 --> 00:49:29.008
Ben!

567
00:49:30.878 --> 00:49:33.004
What's up, son?
What happened?

568
00:49:33.078 --> 00:49:35.136
Are you okay?

569
00:49:35.213 --> 00:49:37.371
Just look at you!

570
00:49:39.212 --> 00:49:41.235
Is everything okay?
What's the matter?

571
00:49:41.312 --> 00:49:44.972
What's the matter
with you, Ben?

572
00:49:47.111 --> 00:49:49.771
That'll do, son.

573
00:49:50.844 --> 00:49:52.401
It's nothing, Mom.

574
00:49:52.478 --> 00:49:53.705
That's what people
always say, it's nothing.

575
00:49:53.778 --> 00:49:57.541
I'm healed, Mom.
I'm really healed.

576
00:49:57.611 --> 00:50:00.100
Completely healed.

577
00:50:02.312 --> 00:50:06.142
Your big brother
is Superman!

578
00:50:06.212 --> 00:50:09.667
Calm down, Ben,
please!

579
00:50:09.745 --> 00:50:11.336
That's enough!

580
00:50:16.945 --> 00:50:20.707
There's water coming
out of your eyes, Mom.

581
00:50:20.778 --> 00:50:23.370
Water is coming
out of your eyes

582
00:50:23.445 --> 00:50:26.002
but I know what it is.
Salt and moisture.

583
00:50:26.078 --> 00:50:28.636
Salt and moisture!

584
00:50:30.412 --> 00:50:33.378
People say
I don't understand

585
00:50:33.445 --> 00:50:35.502
because I don't understand
feelings, but I do.

586
00:50:35.579 --> 00:50:37.807
I know what they are.

587
00:50:37.879 --> 00:50:41.209
Do you remember
when I was little

588
00:50:41.279 --> 00:50:44.268
I tried to push
those tears

589
00:50:44.346 --> 00:50:46.402
back into your eyes?

590
00:50:46.478 --> 00:50:48.671
It was just because
I didn't want you to be sad.

591
00:50:56.045 --> 00:50:58.307
It's all right, Mom.
People always say

592
00:50:58.378 --> 00:51:02.401
it's all right
and they ask,

593
00:51:02.478 --> 00:51:05.001
"ls everything all right?"

594
00:51:05.079 --> 00:51:07.601
And then you reply,
"Yes, yes!

595
00:51:07.679 --> 00:51:10.407
"Yes, everything's all right.
Everything is right.

596
00:51:10.479 --> 00:51:13.672
Everything's going right."

597
00:51:13.745 --> 00:51:16.302
Everything's all right.
Everything's going right.

598
00:51:16.378 --> 00:51:19.969
- I'm not crazy.
- No!

599
00:51:20.045 --> 00:51:23.808
- Just a bit difficult.
- Calm down, Ben.

600
00:51:23.879 --> 00:51:25.640
Yes, I'm a different cult.

601
00:51:25.712 --> 00:51:28.837
But I'm training myself.

602
00:51:28.911 --> 00:51:31.037
I'm training, training,
training.

603
00:51:33.378 --> 00:51:36.071
I'm in bits.

604
00:51:36.145 --> 00:51:37.634
But I've been reborn,

605
00:51:37.712 --> 00:51:39.802
Iike in video games.

606
00:51:41.278 --> 00:51:44.767
- You always get a new life.
- Come on, son.

607
00:51:44.845 --> 00:51:46.970
Let's go home.

608
00:51:47.046 --> 00:51:49.341
Come on, son.
That's it.

609
00:51:55.911 --> 00:51:58.377
And then it was over.

610
00:51:58.445 --> 00:52:01.673
I was over.

611
00:52:01.745 --> 00:52:04.540
Eyes open again,
head shut once more.

612
00:52:04.612 --> 00:52:06.442
Ben.

613
00:52:13.712 --> 00:52:15.177
What's that, Ben?

614
00:52:17.213 --> 00:52:19.576
Why didn't you tell me?

615
00:52:24.978 --> 00:52:27.104
- Ben...
- Then it was time for truthfulness.

616
00:52:29.479 --> 00:52:31.035
Shamefulness, painfulness.

617
00:52:31.111 --> 00:52:33.044
Who did that?

618
00:52:33.112 --> 00:52:34.702
Tell me, Ben.

619
00:52:52.212 --> 00:52:55.337
Everything can be
destroyed so easily.

620
00:52:55.412 --> 00:52:58.207
Everything can be
destroyed so easily.

621
00:52:59.545 --> 00:53:02.238
Why couldn't I just be
destroyed too?

622
00:53:07.679 --> 00:53:10.907
Stop it, Ben.
Stop it!

623
00:53:20.612 --> 00:53:22.374
Jonas!

624
00:53:37.278 --> 00:53:39.108
Jonas.

625
00:53:49.079 --> 00:53:51.010
Then I saw that jerk

626
00:53:51.078 --> 00:53:53.636
standing there again.

627
00:53:53.712 --> 00:53:56.405
And I attacked him.

628
00:54:04.579 --> 00:54:07.204
I'd heard it before,
the calling

629
00:54:07.278 --> 00:54:09.710
of night falling.

630
00:54:09.779 --> 00:54:13.211
Going right
to the end of pain.

631
00:54:14.711 --> 00:54:17.405
How beautiful!
Blood flowing from a vein.

632
00:54:44.011 --> 00:54:46.375
A bit later

633
00:54:46.445 --> 00:54:49.878
my father came round.

634
00:54:49.946 --> 00:54:51.639
My dad,

635
00:54:51.712 --> 00:54:55.042
who also never knows
what to say.

636
00:54:56.679 --> 00:54:59.009
So I usually
understand him that way.

637
00:55:13.378 --> 00:55:16.833
She'd come too.

638
00:55:16.911 --> 00:55:19.878
Sabine, his girlfriend,

639
00:55:19.945 --> 00:55:22.275
as he'd always say.

640
00:55:22.345 --> 00:55:24.868
Who always asked how I was
holding up.

641
00:55:24.946 --> 00:55:27.241
How are you holding up?

642
00:55:30.312 --> 00:55:33.244
- It can't go on like this.
- No, Sabine.

643
00:55:33.312 --> 00:55:34.744
It can't go on like this.

644
00:55:34.812 --> 00:55:38.539
But still, it will have to.
It will have to.

645
00:55:38.612 --> 00:55:41.874
It's not the first time
and it won't be the last.

646
00:55:41.946 --> 00:55:45.503
Come on, Sabine. Leave it.
It's okay, leave it.

647
00:55:49.012 --> 00:55:51.342
Look after him.

648
00:56:00.946 --> 00:56:03.537
The endgame.

649
00:56:03.612 --> 00:56:05.441
The end, the end,
the end, the end.

650
00:56:05.512 --> 00:56:07.842
The end, the end,
the end.

651
00:56:07.912 --> 00:56:11.435
The end, the end,
the end, the end.

652
00:56:11.512 --> 00:56:13.876
The endgame.

653
00:56:13.946 --> 00:56:16.002
The endgame.

654
00:56:16.078 --> 00:56:19.805
Heart rate: 55.

655
00:56:19.878 --> 00:56:23.777
Under 13
and you're dead.

656
00:56:23.845 --> 00:56:27.300
42 to go.

657
00:56:27.379 --> 00:56:30.776
Then you've done it.
You're finished.

658
00:56:30.845 --> 00:56:33.811
42 heartbeats less

659
00:56:33.879 --> 00:56:36.640
and you arrive.
Where there's death, there's life.

660
00:56:36.712 --> 00:56:38.644
You can't play an endgame
without your healer

661
00:56:38.712 --> 00:56:41.769
and that's me.

662
00:56:41.845 --> 00:56:44.436
Tomorrow I'll catch a train that gets
to where you live at 10:22.

663
00:56:44.512 --> 00:56:48.205
- And I know you'll be there...
- 9:36.

664
00:56:48.278 --> 00:56:50.540
Got to go
to the station.

665
00:56:52.445 --> 00:56:54.877
I've got to go
to the station.

666
00:57:09.545 --> 00:57:11.477
Calm down.
Calm down, Ben.

667
00:57:23.545 --> 00:57:24.704
GONE OUT
DON'T WORRY

668
00:57:30.745 --> 00:57:33.540
I'll keep your phone.

669
00:57:49.413 --> 00:57:51.901
The station.
The station.

670
00:58:21.545 --> 00:58:23.511
10:22, at the station
on the platform.

671
00:58:23.579 --> 00:58:25.671
We'll be there.
We've got to see.

672
00:58:27.645 --> 00:58:29.736
I can't be late.

673
00:58:29.812 --> 00:58:31.505
She shouldn't
have to wait.

674
00:58:31.579 --> 00:58:34.511
She who doesn't know
what I look like, who I am.

675
00:58:34.579 --> 00:58:38.102
That I'm not there.
But them...

676
00:59:03.246 --> 00:59:05.178
I knew I'd find her.

677
00:59:05.246 --> 00:59:07.473
I'd smell her,
like the dog I am.

678
00:59:45.279 --> 00:59:48.676
There she was.

679
00:59:52.579 --> 00:59:55.273
She'd come.

680
00:59:55.346 --> 00:59:57.573
She'd really come.

681
00:59:57.645 --> 01:00:01.203
For real!

682
01:00:01.279 --> 01:00:04.210
She was waiting

683
01:00:04.278 --> 01:00:06.244
for me.

684
01:00:22.579 --> 01:00:24.341
She was sending
a text message.

685
01:00:24.413 --> 01:00:26.275
Probably to me.

686
01:00:26.345 --> 01:00:30.437
To me about whom she can only fantasize,
whom she doesn't recognize.

687
01:00:30.512 --> 01:00:33.909
To me who is here
with a phone that's disappeared.

688
01:00:39.445 --> 01:00:41.707
Then everything happened
so quickly, as they say.

689
01:00:41.779 --> 01:00:45.303
But everything always happens
too quickly for me.

690
01:00:45.378 --> 01:00:46.639
She left.

691
01:00:46.712 --> 01:00:48.940
Because she couldn't see

692
01:00:49.012 --> 01:00:50.910
the invisible me.

693
01:00:55.146 --> 01:00:58.669
But what my head couldn't do,
my legs were able to.

694
01:01:38.313 --> 01:01:40.040
There's the train.

695
01:01:40.112 --> 01:01:43.908
A spaceship that has come
to collect us from a barren planet.

696
01:01:47.779 --> 01:01:49.870
Courage is everything.

697
01:01:49.946 --> 01:01:52.911
Doing what you thought
you couldn't do.

698
01:02:51.245 --> 01:02:53.803
Her scent was enough.

699
01:02:53.879 --> 01:02:56.743
The scent of a season

700
01:02:56.812 --> 01:02:58.869
that had
yet to be invented

701
01:02:58.945 --> 01:03:01.912
on a continent
still to be discovered,

702
01:03:01.979 --> 01:03:05.308
but that I could smell
miles from the coast.

703
01:03:08.079 --> 01:03:11.203
With her perfect neck
turned towards me,

704
01:03:11.278 --> 01:03:13.404
she was dreaming
up a landscape.

705
01:03:16.379 --> 01:03:21.141
I imagined how
I'd place my lips there,

706
01:03:21.212 --> 01:03:25.441
staking my claim.

707
01:03:25.513 --> 01:03:27.842
My claim to liberation.

708
01:03:29.413 --> 01:03:31.742
Just sitting here
in the warmth from her body,

709
01:03:31.812 --> 01:03:35.540
briefly, everything
was perfect.

710
01:03:35.613 --> 01:03:37.805
This is a passenger
announcement:

711
01:03:37.879 --> 01:03:40.072
We are about to
arrive in Brussels.

712
01:03:44.478 --> 01:03:46.104
Are you okay?

713
01:03:48.780 --> 01:03:52.507
I had to say something.
Anything.

714
01:03:53.779 --> 01:03:56.574
But the only thing I say
is nothing.

715
01:03:57.845 --> 01:03:59.834
All I can do is leave.

716
01:04:23.679 --> 01:04:25.770
And she left.

717
01:04:27.112 --> 01:04:30.339
She just left.

718
01:04:33.679 --> 01:04:36.406
And I just had
to leave too.

719
01:05:10.312 --> 01:05:12.505
I was scared stiff.

720
01:05:12.579 --> 01:05:14.875
A mother feels
these things.

721
01:05:16.612 --> 01:05:19.601
A hundred times
a second I thought,

722
01:05:19.679 --> 01:05:22.702
"Don't let him do
anything stupid.

723
01:05:22.779 --> 01:05:25.041
Please don't let him do

724
01:05:25.112 --> 01:05:27.408
anything stupid."

725
01:05:27.479 --> 01:05:29.467
I remember
he once asked me,

726
01:05:29.545 --> 01:05:31.603
"How many reasons
does someone need

727
01:05:31.679 --> 01:05:34.077
to commit suicide?"

728
01:05:34.146 --> 01:05:36.475
I asked him what
he meant by how many.

729
01:05:36.545 --> 01:05:38.875
He said,
"How many? Two, five, 10?"

730
01:05:40.079 --> 01:05:43.806
That's what he was
thinking about.

731
01:05:43.880 --> 01:05:45.742
He wanted to know
if he had enough.

732
01:05:49.612 --> 01:05:53.305
The endgame.
My plan.

733
01:05:53.378 --> 01:05:55.901
The one-word plan.

734
01:05:55.979 --> 01:05:59.877
Murder.
The murder of myself.

735
01:05:59.946 --> 01:06:02.537
Catch the train.

736
01:06:02.612 --> 01:06:05.942
To nowhere.

737
01:06:09.378 --> 01:06:11.242
There is one advantage
to killing yourself.

738
01:06:13.012 --> 01:06:15.842
You never have
to look far for your victim.

739
01:06:15.912 --> 01:06:17.775
You don't even
do it yourself,

740
01:06:17.845 --> 01:06:19.640
the train does it for you.

741
01:06:19.712 --> 01:06:23.008
What was his motive?
A locomotive.

742
01:07:08.445 --> 01:07:10.639
If you think
it's all over quickly,

743
01:07:10.712 --> 01:07:13.042
you're wrong.

744
01:07:15.213 --> 01:07:18.645
Even if you're
lucky enough

745
01:07:18.712 --> 01:07:20.735
to be decapitated
immediately,

746
01:07:20.812 --> 01:07:22.539
apparently your head
remains conscious

747
01:07:22.612 --> 01:07:25.442
for another
13 to 15 seconds.

748
01:07:27.712 --> 01:07:31.201
So you can imagine that what goes
through your mind isn't pleasant.

749
01:07:32.613 --> 01:07:35.407
Seeing bits of your body
flying in all directions.

750
01:07:39.912 --> 01:07:43.708
They say that
just before you die...

751
01:07:45.046 --> 01:07:48.273
your life flashes
before your eyes like a film.

752
01:07:48.345 --> 01:07:50.437
So?
Did you see anything?

753
01:07:50.513 --> 01:07:54.001
- But who...
- Who pushed you?

754
01:07:55.345 --> 01:07:59.210
Me, of course.
Who else, blockhead?

755
01:08:02.680 --> 01:08:05.236
You?

756
01:08:05.312 --> 01:08:07.676
Does he have
any distinguishing scars

757
01:08:07.745 --> 01:08:09.541
or birthmarks?

758
01:08:09.613 --> 01:08:11.044
Scars?

759
01:08:12.813 --> 01:08:15.677
It was already broken,
wasn't it?

760
01:08:17.612 --> 01:08:20.908
Did you notice anything
out of the ordinary?

761
01:08:30.679 --> 01:08:32.612
I don't get it, Ben.

762
01:08:32.680 --> 01:08:34.668
Honestly.

763
01:08:38.646 --> 01:08:39.975
Ben.

764
01:08:41.679 --> 01:08:45.544
Are you the man who escaped
from the dungeon of Silancium?

765
01:08:47.445 --> 01:08:51.343
Who crossed Windrill Desert
alone with me?

766
01:08:51.412 --> 01:08:54.742
Who fought Bailor?
Who crossed the swamps

767
01:08:54.812 --> 01:08:58.074
of Ondekon with me?
Who conquered zerdin?

768
01:09:00.279 --> 01:09:03.574
You're level 80,
for God's sake.

769
01:09:07.146 --> 01:09:09.374
And that's your endgame?

770
01:09:09.446 --> 01:09:12.344
You just throw yourself
under a train?

771
01:09:14.813 --> 01:09:17.210
Was that your plan?

772
01:09:18.746 --> 01:09:21.939
Just click on exit
and log out.

773
01:09:25.946 --> 01:09:28.344
"Gone out.
Don't worry. "

774
01:09:28.413 --> 01:09:30.878
That's good news,

775
01:09:30.946 --> 01:09:32.878
isn't it?

776
01:09:32.946 --> 01:09:35.640
It means he's gone out
for a bit and you don't have to worry.

777
01:09:35.713 --> 01:09:37.941
My son doesn't
just go out for a bit

778
01:09:38.013 --> 01:09:41.240
on a Saturday morning.
He's not able to.

779
01:09:42.979 --> 01:09:46.570
Besides, look.
I found this.

780
01:10:04.178 --> 01:10:06.304
I don't know
if you know, Ben, but...

781
01:10:09.545 --> 01:10:12.535
in real life

782
01:10:12.612 --> 01:10:16.510
dying is fairly definite.

783
01:10:19.478 --> 01:10:21.910
You can't change
your mind.

784
01:10:25.079 --> 01:10:27.011
You can die
as much as you like.

785
01:10:28.779 --> 01:10:31.973
But not for real.

786
01:10:32.046 --> 01:10:33.671
That's not the way
we play, Ben.

787
01:10:35.413 --> 01:10:37.538
You're level 80.

788
01:10:40.278 --> 01:10:42.404
Do you want to quit
this world, Ben?

789
01:10:43.512 --> 01:10:44.706
Go on then, go.

790
01:10:46.545 --> 01:10:50.204
But if you want revenge,
take revenge.

791
01:10:53.312 --> 01:10:55.801
Otherwise you're exactly
what they say you are,

792
01:10:55.879 --> 01:10:58.038
a loser.

793
01:10:58.112 --> 01:11:00.168
Play to win, Ben.

794
01:11:02.046 --> 01:11:04.205
Everything's
a matter of planning,

795
01:11:04.279 --> 01:11:07.211
of strategy.

796
01:11:08.879 --> 01:11:10.970
Don't you
just love Fanta?

797
01:11:30.646 --> 01:11:32.271
I'm really happy...

798
01:11:35.179 --> 01:11:37.338
that you're you.

799
01:11:39.579 --> 01:11:42.137
We'll file a missing
person's report

800
01:11:42.213 --> 01:11:45.838
and circulate his
description nationally.

801
01:11:45.912 --> 01:11:47.173
What about this?

802
01:11:47.246 --> 01:11:49.041
What are you going to do
about this?

803
01:11:49.112 --> 01:11:51.907
I'll inform our
social services unit.

804
01:11:51.979 --> 01:11:54.877
They're familiar
with things like that,

805
01:11:54.946 --> 01:11:56.037
unfortunately.

806
01:12:23.979 --> 01:12:25.275
Ben!

807
01:12:44.213 --> 01:12:47.202
"l just wanted to go away,"
he said.

808
01:12:47.279 --> 01:12:51.405
"But I didn't dare die
because I didn't know what that was."

809
01:13:00.912 --> 01:13:03.344
Was that your big plan?

810
01:13:07.779 --> 01:13:09.904
Ben?

811
01:13:09.979 --> 01:13:11.842
How are we going
to do it?

812
01:13:15.780 --> 01:13:17.473
Take poison?

813
01:13:20.679 --> 01:13:21.872
No.

814
01:13:21.946 --> 01:13:26.003
Imagine if you took poison
and then changed your mind.

815
01:13:26.079 --> 01:13:28.136
You'd have to call
the Poison Center.

816
01:13:28.213 --> 01:13:30.610
"Hello?"

817
01:13:38.479 --> 01:13:40.069
The people
at the Poison Center

818
01:13:40.146 --> 01:13:43.408
get lots of phone calls
like that.

819
01:13:47.712 --> 01:13:50.178
That's for idiots.

820
01:13:53.779 --> 01:13:56.473
Or you could hang
yourself.

821
01:13:56.546 --> 01:14:00.069
That's cool. Apparently you die
with a huge erection.

822
01:14:02.513 --> 01:14:05.002
But then
you shit yourself.

823
01:14:05.080 --> 01:14:08.068
That's not cool
being found like that, eh?

824
01:14:10.046 --> 01:14:11.272
Ben.

825
01:14:11.345 --> 01:14:14.335
Do you know what else
they always find

826
01:14:14.412 --> 01:14:17.072
under the fingernails
of someone

827
01:14:17.146 --> 01:14:19.578
who's hung themselves?

828
01:14:19.646 --> 01:14:22.873
Little bits of rope

829
01:14:22.946 --> 01:14:25.072
and skin.

830
01:14:25.146 --> 01:14:26.941
Do you know why?

831
01:14:28.013 --> 01:14:29.478
Because they
always desperately try

832
01:14:29.546 --> 01:14:32.603
to get the rope
off their neck.

833
01:14:32.680 --> 01:14:34.669
But they can't.
The chair's too far away

834
01:14:34.746 --> 01:14:37.438
and they can't reach it.

835
01:14:39.812 --> 01:14:42.778
You think it's exciting,
huh, Ben?

836
01:14:44.246 --> 01:14:46.178
Dying.

837
01:14:46.246 --> 01:14:48.008
Dying.

838
01:14:50.112 --> 01:14:51.738
Then everything is solved
in one fell swoop.

839
01:14:51.813 --> 01:14:54.836
Ben is solved
in one fell swoop.

840
01:14:56.379 --> 01:14:59.970
Aren't you going to take
one last look

841
01:15:00.046 --> 01:15:01.535
to see if there's
another solution?

842
01:15:01.613 --> 01:15:04.408
Take one last
look around.

843
01:15:07.378 --> 01:15:10.742
You need to be more
creative, damn you!

844
01:15:10.813 --> 01:15:13.142
Shut up, beautiful.

845
01:15:13.213 --> 01:15:15.872
You are so beautiful.

846
01:15:17.546 --> 01:15:19.444
"Assemble a guild," she said.

847
01:15:19.513 --> 01:15:22.740
"Like in Archlord."

848
01:15:22.812 --> 01:15:24.745
It was her idea.

849
01:15:24.813 --> 01:15:28.245
Some quests are too big
for two.

850
01:15:38.713 --> 01:15:41.304
"You have to help me,"
he said.

851
01:15:49.946 --> 01:15:52.878
So we helped him.

852
01:15:52.946 --> 01:15:56.537
We knew everyone would say
that you can't do that.

853
01:15:56.612 --> 01:16:00.205
But that's more or less

854
01:16:00.279 --> 01:16:03.074
why I did it.

855
01:16:46.346 --> 01:16:48.743
Smoking's forbidden here,
Sabrina.

856
01:16:48.812 --> 01:16:50.540
My name's Sabine.

857
01:16:53.580 --> 01:16:57.239
You should be grateful
for not being able to smoke.

858
01:16:57.313 --> 01:16:59.871
Yeah,
I'm really grateful.

859
01:16:59.947 --> 01:17:03.379
You'll live half
a day longer.

860
01:17:13.646 --> 01:17:15.736
You're not serious,
right?

861
01:17:15.812 --> 01:17:17.335
You're not really
going to do this!

862
01:17:17.413 --> 01:17:20.140
You know you can't!

863
01:17:20.213 --> 01:17:21.406
I can't do it!

864
01:17:21.479 --> 01:17:23.707
Sabine, you don't have
to do anything.

865
01:17:23.780 --> 01:17:25.745
You insisted on coming.

866
01:17:25.812 --> 01:17:28.835
I don't care whether
you come or not

867
01:17:28.912 --> 01:17:32.777
but if you think
it's easy for us,

868
01:17:32.846 --> 01:17:34.811
you're wrong.

869
01:17:39.546 --> 01:17:41.375
Look.

870
01:17:44.979 --> 01:17:46.707
The sea.

871
01:17:49.113 --> 01:17:51.577
The end of the world.

872
01:17:53.780 --> 01:17:56.712
You know what
they say, Ben?

873
01:17:56.780 --> 01:17:59.610
Every end is a beginning.

874
01:18:14.246 --> 01:18:16.678
Anyone want anything to eat?
Ben?

875
01:18:16.746 --> 01:18:19.712
- Sabine?
- No, thanks.

876
01:18:19.780 --> 01:18:21.109
Don't you feel very well,
Sabine?

877
01:18:21.179 --> 01:18:23.145
Not really, no.

878
01:18:24.679 --> 01:18:27.941
Is this how you want
it to be, Ben?

879
01:18:29.479 --> 01:18:32.002
Right.

880
01:18:38.279 --> 01:18:41.109
Ben, uh--
I'll...

881
01:18:42.213 --> 01:18:44.236
Ben!
Ben!

882
01:18:56.313 --> 01:18:59.075
I have to put my back into it.

883
01:19:00.413 --> 01:19:02.641
Everything is a matter
of thinking ahead.

884
01:19:02.713 --> 01:19:06.702
And thinking a-heart.

885
01:19:06.779 --> 01:19:10.041
Everything is a matter
of willpower.

886
01:19:33.812 --> 01:19:36.677
Courage is everything.

887
01:19:38.346 --> 01:19:40.743
Ultimately doing the thing

888
01:19:40.812 --> 01:19:43.642
that you can't do.

889
01:20:06.479 --> 01:20:09.001
If you die in a game

890
01:20:09.079 --> 01:20:12.409
then you're just
out of the game for a while

891
01:20:12.479 --> 01:20:15.911
and you have to go
and look for your body.

892
01:20:20.947 --> 01:20:24.141
All they found of me
was a tape.

893
01:20:25.713 --> 01:20:29.338
And I had gone.

894
01:20:42.580 --> 01:20:45.546
These are particularly
disturbing images

895
01:20:45.613 --> 01:20:48.238
that once again remind us

896
01:20:48.313 --> 01:20:51.336
that one Flemish youngster
takes his or her life every week.

897
01:20:51.413 --> 01:20:54.777
In a recent study,
10% of Flemish youngsters

898
01:20:54.846 --> 01:20:57.607
between 15 and 18

899
01:20:57.680 --> 01:21:01.168
say that they have attempted
suicide at some point.

900
01:21:01.246 --> 01:21:04.269
A very worrying figure.

901
01:21:04.346 --> 01:21:05.902
And now the sports.

902
01:21:05.979 --> 01:21:08.502
At the lndian Wells
tournament...

903
01:21:08.979 --> 01:21:11.104
Everyone here today,

904
01:21:11.179 --> 01:21:13.805
members of the family,

905
01:21:13.880 --> 01:21:17.210
colleagues,

906
01:21:17.279 --> 01:21:20.439
Iadies and gentlemen,
girls and boys...

907
01:21:21.780 --> 01:21:24.110
we've all come
together today

908
01:21:24.179 --> 01:21:25.974
to say goodbye

909
01:21:26.046 --> 01:21:29.012
to a very special young man

910
01:21:29.079 --> 01:21:33.512
who was taken from us

911
01:21:33.580 --> 01:21:36.273
so suddenly

912
01:21:36.346 --> 01:21:39.335
and tragically.

913
01:21:39.413 --> 01:21:42.311
Ben's life was never easy.

914
01:21:42.379 --> 01:21:46.277
His condition made things

915
01:21:46.347 --> 01:21:50.403
very difficult for him.

916
01:21:51.513 --> 01:21:54.138
Maybe

917
01:21:54.213 --> 01:21:56.941
we only realize now,

918
01:21:57.013 --> 01:22:01.206
when it's too late,

919
01:22:01.279 --> 01:22:05.938
that he battled against
his handicap,

920
01:22:06.012 --> 01:22:08.501
if you can call it that,

921
01:22:08.580 --> 01:22:10.977
that was much worse
than we could've imagined.

922
01:22:11.046 --> 01:22:15.240
We never really
had any real contact with him

923
01:22:15.313 --> 01:22:17.972
and won't be able to now.

924
01:22:18.046 --> 01:22:22.672
Today all we can do
is accept

925
01:22:22.746 --> 01:22:24.041
that some things

926
01:22:24.112 --> 01:22:27.135
are just
too heavy to bear.

927
01:22:28.546 --> 01:22:31.773
That is why...

928
01:22:31.845 --> 01:22:33.539
Hello.

929
01:22:33.613 --> 01:22:37.705
Thank you for coming.

930
01:22:37.780 --> 01:22:40.746
I too have come
to an end,

931
01:22:40.813 --> 01:22:42.870
as they say.

932
01:22:42.947 --> 01:22:45.208
Come to an end.

933
01:22:45.279 --> 01:22:48.575
I died of myself.

934
01:22:48.645 --> 01:22:51.975
Fellow men

935
01:22:52.046 --> 01:22:53.672
and un-fellow men...

936
01:22:56.113 --> 01:22:57.772
my fight is over.

937
01:23:02.046 --> 01:23:05.137
At the end of your life,
they say a film

938
01:23:05.213 --> 01:23:09.112
of your life flashes
before your eyes.

939
01:23:09.180 --> 01:23:12.271
Here are a few scenes

940
01:23:12.347 --> 01:23:14.278
that may interest you.

941
01:24:54.813 --> 01:24:56.711
Go on, Ben.

942
01:24:56.779 --> 01:24:59.245
Now, the endgame.

943
01:25:59.946 --> 01:26:03.242
She called it dying creatively.

944
01:26:03.313 --> 01:26:07.178
Suicide without the dying.

945
01:26:07.247 --> 01:26:10.236
Dying without quitting.

946
01:26:10.314 --> 01:26:14.575
Or quitting without dying.

947
01:26:15.946 --> 01:26:18.435
I had to learn everything.

948
01:26:18.513 --> 01:26:21.775
But I'd forgotten
the most important thing.

949
01:26:23.314 --> 01:26:25.074
Learning to lie.

950
01:26:26.413 --> 01:26:29.607
To deceive.

951
01:26:44.446 --> 01:26:47.503
Someone had to die first.

952
01:26:47.580 --> 01:26:50.774
Otherwise you wouldn't
have come.

953
01:26:52.213 --> 01:26:55.736
Not for a boy.

954
01:26:58.845 --> 01:27:02.710
You can't keep on
begging and asking...

955
01:27:02.780 --> 01:27:05.405
You're so angry, Mommy.

956
01:27:05.479 --> 01:27:07.445
And asking again and again

957
01:27:07.513 --> 01:27:10.809
that something be done
to put a stop to it.

958
01:27:10.880 --> 01:27:14.573
That they'd finally stop

959
01:27:14.646 --> 01:27:17.476
tormenting my son

960
01:27:17.546 --> 01:27:22.240
and making his life--

961
01:27:22.313 --> 01:27:24.506
sorry, but it's true--

962
01:27:24.580 --> 01:27:26.808
making his life
so impossible.

963
01:27:26.880 --> 01:27:30.812
His autism is his problem,
but it's not a problem to him.

964
01:27:30.880 --> 01:27:33.971
The others are the problem.
The others.

965
01:27:34.047 --> 01:27:37.138
They have to learn

966
01:27:38.279 --> 01:27:40.871
to leave my kid alone.

967
01:27:40.947 --> 01:27:44.140
Ben just wanted to quit.
Now he has.

968
01:27:46.047 --> 01:27:49.570
Fortunately,
he's still alive.

969
01:27:51.112 --> 01:27:54.545
He's alive.

970
01:27:54.613 --> 01:27:57.579
In his own world, maybe,
but he's alive.

971
01:27:57.646 --> 01:27:59.340
He's alive!

972
01:28:01.613 --> 01:28:03.011
He's living his life.

973
01:28:08.413 --> 01:28:10.379
She said,

974
01:28:10.446 --> 01:28:14.004
"It's high time
to become who you are."

975
01:28:24.079 --> 01:28:25.137
Just let it happen, Ben.

976
01:28:27.446 --> 01:28:29.140
Don't be scared.

977
01:28:37.146 --> 01:28:38.737
If you want
to learn to feel good,

978
01:28:38.813 --> 01:28:40.836
you have to learn to feel.

979
01:28:40.912 --> 01:28:42.435
Stroke him.

980
01:28:46.013 --> 01:28:49.775
I've never been
what they call happy.

981
01:28:49.846 --> 01:28:52.005
But I've never been

982
01:28:52.080 --> 01:28:55.240
this kind of happy.

983
01:29:01.947 --> 01:29:05.243
Beautiful, no?
You don't have to talk to animals.

984
01:29:05.314 --> 01:29:09.405
Do you dare sit on it,
you two-bit hero?

985
01:29:12.013 --> 01:29:15.536
As soon as people
see a horse,

986
01:29:15.613 --> 01:29:17.943
they want to sit on it.

987
01:29:18.013 --> 01:29:20.274
But has anyone
ever heard a horse

988
01:29:20.346 --> 01:29:24.210
ask for that?
Do you?

989
01:29:24.279 --> 01:29:27.677
If a horse could choose...

990
01:29:32.680 --> 01:29:36.010
Yes, well...
